## 4. Data Points and Quotes the Advocate Must Address

- **NFPA 72 threshold, direct:** “Intelligibility of an emergency communication system is considered acceptable if at least 90 percent of the measurement locations within each ADS have a measured STI of not less than 0.45 and an average STI of not less than 0.50” [Source: https://www.suppressionsystems.com/voice-intelligibility-in-mass-notification-systems/]. The advocate must show what the MWAA standard adds *above* this code floor and why the addition is worth the governance load.
- **London City’s own carve-outs:** LCY silent policy explicitly retains PA for “gate changes at short notice, during disruption (when there are cancelled or delayed flights) and when there is a flight information display failure” [Source: https://www.londoncityairport.com/silent-airport-policy]. The advocate must explain how a MWAA standard performs better than “PA on for the worst 10% of days,” which is what LCY has actually built.
- **Copenhagen documented failure mode:** A CPH passenger review reports: “the airport doesn’t put out calls… there are no screens in the passport gate so passengers cannot see updates” and describes a missed transatlantic flight [Source: https://www.trustpilot.com/review/www.cph.dk]. The advocate must reconcile the CPH exemplar with the operational failure mode CPH itself produces at scale.
- **NTSB DCA finding:** “The NTSB believes the word ‘circling’ was inaudible, possibly contributing to the pilots’ confusion” [Source: https://www.npr.org/2026/01/27/nx-s1-5689091/ntsb-dca-midair-collision-black-hawk-helicopter]. The advocate must confront the fact that MWAA’s home region has just spent 2025–26 litigating a communications-inaudibility fatality with 67 dead, and must show why a standard branded as quiet-by-design will not be received in that context as a policy going the wrong way.
- **The capital calendar:** Concourse E opens autumn 2026; DCA Terminal 2 refresh is in the field; the $20–22.5B Dulles expansion has no disclosed funding structure and its C/D replacement designs are years from IFC [context packet; Source: https://parametric-architecture.com/trumps-22-5-billion-dulles-airport]. The advocate must name the specific near-term project whose design gate the standard actually catches.

